WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:04.960
Marvel's "What If...?" is all about reimagining
the MCU as we know it.

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:09.890
Episode 1 saw Peggy Carter become the world's
first supersoldier instead of Steve Rogers,

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:13.970
while Episode 2 saw T'Challa as Star-Lord
instead of Peter Quill.

00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:17.730
However, for Episode 3, it's more than just
a simple substitution.

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:22.480
The story revolves around the Avengers and
Nick Fury's quest to bring the group together.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:26.050
Simply put, the question we're meant to ask
ourselves in this episode is, "What if the

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:28.100
Avengers never happened?"

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:29.200
"Wow.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:31.390
So serious."

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:36.510
The episode primarily focuses on how the Avengers
are picked off one by one; even the strongest

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:41.300
and seemingly immortal ones get their tails
handed to them in one shocking death after

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:42.300
the next.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:45.600
First, Tony Stark is killed by Natasha Romanoff
accidentally.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.309
Then, Clint Barton inadvertently takes out
Thor, with the archer's death following in

00:00:50.309 --> 00:00:52.389
a prison cell shortly after.

00:00:52.389 --> 00:00:56.980
The Hulk is the next to meet his end in rather
gruesome death, and sadly, we say goodbye

00:00:56.980 --> 00:01:00.999
to Natasha -- again -- as she's the last of
the group to bite the bullet.

00:01:00.999 --> 00:01:05.089
For most of the episode, we wonder who is
the person behind these attacks, and while

00:01:05.089 --> 00:01:09.670
they weren't exactly hiding in plain sight,
they were right in front of us the whole time.

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:12.900
"What a fascinating choice of words."

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:17.299
Natasha figures out the mysterious killer
after logging into some SHIELD files at a

00:01:17.299 --> 00:01:18.820
public library.

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:24.159
She realizes that Hope Van Dyne had also logged
into the system, despite being dead for two

00:01:24.159 --> 00:01:25.159
years.

00:01:25.159 --> 00:01:28.420
After hearing Natasha screaming to him on
the phone that it's "all about Hope," Nick

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:32.539
Fury heads to the Wasp's gravesite, where
he's met by her father, Hank Pym.

00:01:32.539 --> 00:01:36.939
Looking absolutely haggard, Hank is revealed
as the killer of all five Avengers.

00:01:36.939 --> 00:01:40.890
We then get a small flashback of the deaths
of the would-be Avengers where we see tiny

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:44.960
little Hank in his Ant-Man outfit killing
all of the would-be superheroes — so the

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:48.939
fact that we couldn't see the killer the whole
time should have been a dead giveaway.

00:01:48.939 --> 00:01:54.369
It turns out Hank is exacting revenge on SHIELD
for the death of his daughter, who, Fury explains,

00:01:54.369 --> 00:01:57.460
died outside of Ukraine during a mission for
the agency.

00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:02.840
Hank blames SHIELD for her death and decides
the appropriate revenge is killing five people,

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:06.510
wanting Fury to see everything he's worked
for regarding the Avengers die.

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:08.330
"You never cared about Hope!"

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:10.000
"I don't give a damn about any of 'em!"

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:14.790
In a shocking twist no one could see coming,
Fury takes down the man who killed five Avengers

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:16.400
— with the help of Loki.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:20.780
The God of Mischief has already come to Earth
for vengeance after learning of Thor's death,

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:23.980
but Fury convinces him to give him more time
to find the killer.

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:28.840
With the help of Loki's magic, Fury has the
upper hand over Hank, and the latter is eventually

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:30.340
taken into custody.

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:34.330
Here is where we get to imagine what would
happen in the MCU if Hank killed five of the

00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:35.680
six Avengers.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:39.540
After Fury tells Loki to go back where he
came from, the trickster reveals he wants

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:42.340
to extend his stay on Midgard with a mischievous
grin.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:46.910
We then see Loki give a speech at the United
Nations in New York City, where he appears

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:49.120
to have become the new leader of Earth.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:53.260
Now it's time for a new group of heroes to
assemble to take down Loki, who is living

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:56.370
out the life he only could have dreamed of
in another reality.

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:59.560
"The Avengers fell before they had a chance
to rise.

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:01.390
May they rest in peace."

00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:02.520
"They can.

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:04.870
But we won't."

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:09.010
As you watch the episode and the poor Avengers
get picked off one by one, you might wonder

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:10.670
where Captain America was.

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:14.330
Well, he was still doing time as a capsicle
under the ice.

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:18.370
Fury also puts a call out on his favorite
pager while dusting the snow off of Cap's

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:19.370
frozen shield.

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:23.410
At the end of the episode, Captain Marvel
pops in, ready for battle.

00:03:23.410 --> 00:03:27.640
So we now have a team of two Avengers who
will take on Loki as he rules the world with

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:30.160
a loyal army of Asgardians behind him.

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:35.200
In this reality, things are vastly different
than we know them from the Infinity Saga timeline.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:40.430
Knocking out Natasha, Thor, the Hulk, Iron
Man, and Hawkeye means only a few superpeople

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:42.650
and worthy SHIELD agents are left.

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:46.770
Based on this timeline and the story of Hope
Van Dyne and Hank Pym, we can assume that

00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:50.290
Scott Lang is just a regular old criminal
and not Ant-Man.

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:54.600
The Winter Soldier is still out there somewhere,
but he likely won't be recruited into a new

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:55.880
Avenger team.

00:03:55.880 --> 00:04:00.310
Spider-Man in this universe isn't around yet,
and the Guardians of the Galaxy have yet to

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:01.380
be formed.

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:05.910
T'Challa also hasn't taken on the mantle of
Black Panther, which means it's slim pickings

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:06.910
for Fury.

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:10.960
It looks like Loki might have a nice run as
ruler of Midgard for quite some time, but

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:13.940
Captain Marvel should be a worthy adversary
of the trickster.

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:18.700
Together with Steve Rogers, the pair might
be able to take him down, but only if Fury

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:21.120
can find them some strong sidekicks.

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:25.230
This episode really has us wondering what
it will take for the Watcher to get involved.

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:29.340
If killing five Avengers doesn't encourage
him to step in, what will?

